A cyberattack on Danish company Danfoss’s software has disrupted refrigeration systems at around 150 Intermarché stores and 80 Carrefour outlets across France. 

The attack reportedly caused refrigerator temperatures to rise to 50°C, spoiling food and sparking fires at some locations.

