United Airlines, Air France adopt Israeli ban affecting pilots from Muslim countries

United Airlines, a major American carrier, and Air France, France's national airline, have agreed to implement an Israeli directive barring pilots and cabin crew from countries with no formal diplomatic relations with Israel from operating flights entering the airspace above the occupied territories.

